389|/***
390| * MARK: recordTimelineWithDiffStat
391| * @description Records a stage-transition timeline entry immediately, then
392| *   best-effort attributes a per-stage `+N -M` badge once git answers. Stays
393| *   synchronous for its callers (stage transitions, failure routing): the
394| *   entry is always recorded, the badge data lands a moment later and the
395| *   markdown is re-saved. The badge shows only the lines changed while that
396| *   stage was active (current cumulative minus the previous row's baseline),
397| *   so a no-op stage renders `+0 -0` while a genuinely unknown diff (git
398| *   failure) renders no badge. Any git failure means "no badge", never a
399| *   failed transition. Deferred backfills run in call order per task, so a
400| *   rapid enter → fail sequence cannot misattribute baselines. When the task
