681| * @description Extracts the `# Goal` section body from a task.md body. The goal
682| *   ends at the first terminator heading (`# History`, `# Timeline`,
683| *   `# Process Logs`, `# Log Entries`; surrounding whitespace ignored) that is
684| *   OUTSIDE a fenced code block, so heading-like example text inside a ` ``` `
685| *   or `~~~` fence (common in rich markdown tasks) never truncates the goal.
686| *   A fence only closes on the same marker character that opened it. If a
687| *   fence is never closed, the scan falls back to the first terminator
688| *   regardless of fences so an unbalanced fence cannot swallow the History
689| *   section. Line endings are normalised to LF. Returns the trimmed goal text
690| *   ("" when there is no `# Goal` section).
691| * @example extractGoalSection("# Goal\nhello\n# History\n- x") => "hello"
692| * @param {string} body - The markdown body after frontmatter.
